If the accused officer is found  
guilty, the board shall make recom­
mendations as- to punishment which  
shall be limited to the following:
(1) Dismissal from the Service;
(2) Reduction of grade;
(3) Reduction of rank number in his  
own grade;
(4) Retention of his present number  
on register for a specified time or until  
a specified number of officers shall have  
been promoted over him;
(5) Official reprimand by circular  
letter;
(6) Official reprimand by Surgeon  
General;
(7) Any combination of (2), (3), (4),  
(5), and (6).

The trial examiner will then close the 
case and make his report upon the facts; 
conclusions of fact; conclusions of law; 
and recommendation for appropriate ac­
tion by the Commission.
